# Agent notes for {{.ProjectName}}

This is an Andurel application. Use the `andurel` CLI to discover the project shape and to read the reference patterns instead of inventing file paths, URLs, or generator names.

Frontend: Inertia ({{.Inertia}}) + Vite. HTTP: `net/http` via `pkg/anduin` — handlers are `func(ctx context.Context) error`. There is no Echo and no Fx. Domains are type-driven: invariants live in newtypes built by `ParseX` constructors; there are no post-construction `Validate` methods.

## Discovery

```bash
andurel commands --json
andurel inspect project --json
andurel inspect handlers --json
andurel inspect domains --json
andurel inspect routes --json
andurel doctor --json
```

## Patterns (read-only)

`andurel patterns` prints reference code, the placement rules, and a "definition of done" checklist. It never writes files; you write every file.

```bash
andurel patterns list
andurel patterns show domain
andurel patterns show service
andurel patterns show handler
andurel patterns show route
andurel patterns show job
andurel patterns show email
andurel patterns show migration
andurel patterns show test-domain
andurel patterns show test-handler
andurel patterns show test-integration
